1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,174
This is the Corsair Queen.

2
00:00:02,624 --> 00:00:06,102
She is not in the game you downloaded.

3
00:00:06,552 --> 00:00:12,639
I wrote her this morning, in one small text file, without writing any code.

4
00:00:13,089 --> 00:00:17,437
In the next fourteen minutes you will write your own.

5
00:00:18,637 --> 00:00:21,246
In Siege, raiders attack your starbases.

6
00:00:21,696 --> 00:00:28,217
If you choose a boss, then when the raiders are nearly beaten, something worse arrives.

7
00:00:28,667 --> 00:00:31,276
Four bosses come with the game.

8
00:00:31,726 --> 00:00:35,639
Each one is a single file in a folder.

9
00:00:36,089 --> 00:00:40,002
Add a file, and you have added a boss.

10
00:00:41,202 --> 00:00:42,941
Here is the Warlord.

11
00:00:43,391 --> 00:00:49,043
Two records, the shape you already know: a heading, a fence, a body.

12
00:00:49,493 --> 00:00:52,102
The first record is the boss.

13
00:00:52,552 --> 00:00:56,030
Boss says what kind of record it is.

14
00:00:56,480 --> 00:01:03,002
Trigger and Low say when she arrives: when a quarter of the raiders are left.

15
00:01:03,452 --> 00:01:06,930
Flies and Fleets say what comes with her.

16
00:01:07,380 --> 00:01:11,728
Difficulty: +1 makes her one step harder than the game.

17
00:01:12,178 --> 00:01:16,961
Named is her flagship: a name, then which ship it is.

18
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:20,770
Never edit the Warlord. Copy it.

19
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:23,828
And not into the game's folder.

20
00:01:24,278 --> 00:01:29,061
The game's folder is replaced every time the game is updated.

21
00:01:29,511 --> 00:01:32,120
Yours is here: common data, bosses.

22
00:01:32,570 --> 00:01:34,309
The Siege reads both.

23
00:01:34,759 --> 00:01:39,107
Lowercase, underscores, no spaces, and keep .amd on the end.

24
00:01:40,307 --> 00:01:43,350
Square brackets are what the crew reads.

25
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:48,583
Round brackets are the key; match your file name." "Two traps.

26
00:01:49,033 --> 00:01:55,554
Lint catches both, and you will see that in a minute, but know them now.

27
00:01:56,004 --> 00:02:05,135
First: if you forget to change the name in square brackets, you get two Warlords and the list shows only one.

28
00:02:05,585 --> 00:02:08,628
Second: the flagship's name is one word.

29
00:02:09,078 --> 00:02:16,035
Type 'Iron Duke' and the game reads a ship called Iron, of a kind called Duke.

30
00:02:16,485 --> 00:02:18,659
There is no such ship.

31
00:02:19,859 --> 00:02:22,902
Now the part you are here for.

32
00:02:23,352 --> 00:02:25,526
One line for her entrance.

33
00:02:25,976 --> 00:02:34,672
Then the objective: a new name, a new key, what it pays, and what you want the crew to read.

34
00:02:35,122 --> 00:02:38,600
Leave the five lines in between alone today.

35
00:02:39,050 --> 00:02:44,702
Plain quotes and plain hyphens only; the game cannot draw the curly kind.

36
00:02:45,902 --> 00:02:46,902
Two checks.

37
00:02:47,352 --> 00:02:49,526
No squiggles in the editor.

38
00:02:49,976 --> 00:02:56,498
Then lint, pointed at my own folder, so it checks my bosses and nothing else.

39
00:02:56,948 --> 00:02:59,122
You want the word 'clean'.

40
00:02:59,572 --> 00:03:10,007
Here is what it says if I put 'Iron Duke' back: it tells me what the game will read, and what to write instead.

41
00:03:11,207 --> 00:03:15,120
Start the server, choose Siege, open the Boss list.

42
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:16,874
There she is.

43
00:03:17,324 --> 00:03:26,020
If she is not, the file is in the wrong folder, or the mission was already running when you saved.

44
00:03:26,470 --> 00:03:29,948
The list is read when the mission starts.

45
00:03:31,148 --> 00:03:37,235
At twenty-five percent you would fight for a long time before she shows up.

46
00:03:37,685 --> 00:03:40,293
For testing, set it to ninety.

47
00:03:40,743 --> 00:03:43,787
Now she comes after the first kills.

48
00:03:44,237 --> 00:03:51,193
There is the Morrigan, there are her escorts, and there is your objective, in your words.

49
00:03:51,643 --> 00:03:55,557
Put Low back to twenty-five when you are done.

50
00:03:56,757 --> 00:03:59,365
This is why she lives here.

51
00:03:59,815 --> 00:04:03,728
Update the game and this folder is left alone.

52
00:04:04,178 --> 00:04:12,439
It is still one file on one computer, so keep a copy, the way you would with a manuscript.

53
00:04:12,889 --> 00:04:16,802
Now make a second boss, from your own story.

54
00:04:17,252 --> 00:04:20,730
The page has the steps and a checklist.

55
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:23,789
Next time, we change the numbers.
